# Matching — one person identity, one email normalize

Do **not** invent a local `email.toLowerCase().trim()` (or similar) when deciding “same person” for Echo, email automation, claim/link, submit, or `sent_matches` lookups.

## Required

1. Use shared helpers from `src/lib/response-dedupe.js`:
   - `normalizeEmailForPersonKey` — canonical email (also when writing `normalized_email`)
   - `personKeyForResponse` / `pickLatestResponsesPerPerson` — who is the same person
   - `responseEmailMatchOrParts` — any PostgREST filter on `email` / `normalized_email` (must match legacy spellings e.g. trailing `.`; values are double-quoted for PostgREST)
2. Remap historical `responses.id` in `sent_matches` / drafts via person key / siblings (`match-person-remap.js`, `loadSiblingResponseIds`) — never assume ids are stable across resubmits.
3. Echo「已通知」comes only from successful `sent_matches` (annotate); do not use raw id-only joins that automation already remaps in memory.

## Why

Email automation grouped people in memory with normalize; Echo used exact DB email strings → same human looked like two people; sent badge and scores diverged.

Full rule + checklist: `docs/matching/PERSON-IDENTITY-AND-EMAIL-NORMALIZE.md`
